Table accounting_settings {
  id          bigint       [pk, increment]
  key         varchar(255) [not null, unique]
  account_id  bigint       [not null]
  description varchar(255) [null]
  created_at  timestamp    [null]
  updated_at  timestamp    [null]

  Note: '''
  Domain: Accounting
  Model: App\Domains\Accounting\Models\AccountingSetting

  Global default COA mappings that drive transaction automation. Key/value
  rather than a one-row-many-columns table so a new mapping is a seeder row,
  not a migration.

  SEEDED KEYS
    default_receivable      -> 1121 Piutang Dagang Client
    default_payable         -> 2110 Hutang Dagang Vendor
    default_vat_input       -> 1141 PPN Masukan
    default_vat_output      -> 2121 PPN Keluaran
    default_income_tax      -> 2122 Hutang PPh Pemotongan
    default_sales_revenue   -> 4100 Pendapatan Sewa Media Iklan
    default_project_expense -> 5100 Beban HPP Sewa Billboard Vendor
    opening_balance_equity  -> 3900 Opening Balance Equity

  Global, NOT per fiscal mode — there is one master COA.

  Changing a mapping only affects transactions created afterwards. Journal
  entries already posted keep pointing at the account they were posted to,
  because they store account_id directly rather than resolving the setting
  at read time. Closed periods therefore never move.

  account_id must reference a LEAF account.
  '''
}

Ref: accounting_settings.account_id > chart_of_accounts.id
